# Allowlist: the image only needs the backend's lockfile, project metadata and
# package (backend/src). Everything else (.git, .venv, .worktrees, data/,
# exports, tests, docs/, .env and other secrets, caches) stays out of the
# build context. TODO(overhaul wave 3): allow frontend/ for the Node stage.
*
!backend/pyproject.toml
!backend/uv.lock
!backend/README.md
!backend/src/

# never ship caches or local runtime data that ended up inside the package
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.DS_Store
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/.env
**/*.env
